  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Tuesday/... \nHigh pressure will briefly build into the region late Saturday \ninto Sunday, bringing a respite from the wet pattern. Valley \nhighs will remain in the upper 40s to low 50s through the \nweekend, generally about 5 to 10 degrees above normal. By \nMonday, an active pattern will return with warm southwest flow \naloft. Models disagree on how far south Canadian cold air will\ntrack, with the current forecast favoring a return to near\nnormal temperatures and a reduction in snow levels across the \nregion back down to 5500-6500 ft through next Tuesday. Models \nthen remain aligned for the next week on a strong closed low \nmoving into California-Nevada on Tuesday. The impact over the \nIntermountain West is slightly more uncertain based on the track\nof the low by the middle of the week. Several deterministic \nsolutions favor this low positioned slightly further north, \nwhich would increase the precipitation forecast substantially by\nlate Tuesday. Other solutions push this low and the moisture \nsouth, which would bring mostly dry conditions through the \nmiddle of the week.",
